      "statusChangeID": null,
      "value": "This isn't a practical idea as \"whitelisted\" scripts must be built into the client which would create a maintenance issue on VRChat's part as it would require VRChat to include every driver into the client, and to update the client every time there was a driver update.\n\nHowever in response to your finger tracking suggestions there is some good news. Valve has recently added a skeletal input API to the OpenVR API (the interface SteamVR uses to communicate with VR applications). This allows VR applications to get a representation of the user's hand skeleton from SteamVR. This means that applications don't need to add support for each type of controller separately, they can instead add support for SteamVR's skeletal input API and then controllers that supply SteamVR with skeletal input data should automatically work.\n\nI expect VRChat will get support for the skeletal input API whenever support for Valve's Knuckles controllers is added.",
      "viewerReactions": null
    },
