  "companyID": "58c62e995865713647a7115d",
  "created": "2018-08-01T06:16:08.179Z",
  "deletedAt": null,
  "details": "It would be great if VRchat would offer a paid for service for companies to get their controller scripts white-listed or a driver supported for use within VRchat. \n\nThe evaluation would take time from the VRChat dev team and so having a monetary return maybe makes it worthwhile to have someone at the team give part of his time just for that one service. \n\nIt's great because it would allow external dev teams to provide some development for VRChat. \n\nAn important aspect in VRChat is control/input and I have no doubt VRChats currently available controls are leaving users wanting more. If the interest is there I would gladly get one of my programmers from my company to write a driver allowing for individual finger bending. Some people with some arduino skills and bend sensors could make their own custom finger controllers and future products would benefit.\n\nI would gladly post the result of this on github if something would come out of this pitch.",
